From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: michael moore <mrmoore27@pm.me>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 03:55:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/27] prime: judge fake DATUM by canaries, not by similarity
 to the pool

Real Knots nodes with converged mempools build near-identical
templates, so the similarity detector flagged honest gateways
(xbt-lead's verify: knots-h1/h2 flagged). Being identical to the
pool is now reported only, never scored.

Canaries convict and clear. Prime hands a gateway's registered node a
canary C, sends P a conflicting twin C' that pays 1 sat more (neither
can replace the other), and tells P never to template C. A gateway
built from P's template cannot carry C. Flagged when at least 10 are
due and fewer than 25 % were templated in time. Timing leads (tx and
tip) can only clear a gateway, because an honest node near the pool
lags it too. With neither signal, independence is 0 and nothing is
flagged.

The Knots path now asserts the verdict: 2 honest + proxy + mimic, 100 %
of traffic entering at P, 3/3 runs green. The demo's primed no longer
outlives the script (exec), and a busy stats port fails the run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
